{"code":"BYN2201","severity":"error","file":"input.byn","span":{"start":35,"end":38,"line":2,"column":17,"endLine":2,"endColumn":20},"message":"a `string` cannot be indexed","label":"strings have no indexer","help":"read a byte, slice, or take characters; `string` is UTF-8, so position 0 is not a character:\n  `name.bytes[0]`       the byte at offset 0 (applied below)\n  `name[a..b]`          the text between byte offsets a and b\n  `name.runes.take(n)`  the first n runes\n  `name.graphemes`      user-perceived characters","fixes":[{"span":{"start":31,"end":38,"line":2,"column":13,"endLine":2,"endColumn":20},"replacement":"name.bytes[0]"}]}
